@Host = https://localhost:7050

### 1. Reset database (Development only)
POST {{Host}}/api/v1/admin/reset-database
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 2. Login with seeded user (Alice) - Save token for next requests
POST {{Host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@principia.edu",
  "password": "dummyhash"
}

### 3. Login with seeded user (Bob)
POST {{Host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "bob@principia.edu",
  "password": "dummyhash"
}

### 4. Test /me endpoint with valid token (replace {{$bearerToken}} with actual token from login response)
GET {{Host}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{$bearerToken}}

### 5. Register a new user
POST {{Host}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User2",
  "email": "test2@principia.edu",
  "password": "dummyhash"
}

### 6. Login with the newly registered user
POST {{Host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test2@principia.edu",
  "password": "dummyhash"
}

### 7. Test login with wrong password (should fail)
POST {{Host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@principia.edu",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### 8. Test login with non-existent user (should fail)
POST {{Host}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@principia.edu",
  "password": "anypassword"
}

### 9. Test /items endpoint (replace {{$bearerToken}} with a valid token)
GET {{Host}}/api/v1/items
Authorization: Bearer {{$bearerToken}}

###

### 10. (Optional) Refresh token (if implemented)
POST {{Host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Authorization: Bearer {{$bearerToken}}

###

@q=string
@house=string
### 11. (Admin) Get users (replace {{$bearerToken}} with an admin token)
GET {{Host}}/api/v1/admin/users?q={{q}}&house={{house}}
Authorization: Bearer {{$bearerToken}}

###